    "claim_allowed": null,
    "claim_withheld_reason": "cnn is better than rf on E. coli at every train size (0 excluded, all three model-init seeds agreeing in sign), but the +-0.02 practical margin is not established anywhere: at the primary size the gap is established to lie in [+0.0047, +0.0161], INSIDE the margin. A conclusive negative, not an unresolved one - and not a licence to claim `cnn > rf` as a finding."
  },
  "status": "rejected",
  "limitations": [
    "margin 0.02 is NOT established at any train size: three sizes are `superior_margin_unresolved` (better, by an amount the interval cannot pin under the bar) and train 2000 is `superior_but_below_margin` (better, and the gap is SHOWN to be under it)",
    "the cnn advantage SHRINKS with data (+0.0320 at 500 -> +0.0104 at 2000), so a claim quoted without its train size would be the misleading version of this result",
    "one dataset (ecoli) and one feature set (one-hot 96x4); no transfer claim is made",
    "6 of 56 series carry the grouped structure the mixed-effects estimator handles (ICC 0.864); this comparison uses the series-unit interval, which is the project's primary metric but not the only defensible unit",
    "3 model-init seeds per arm - enough for the two-component interval the policy requires, not enough to describe the seed distribution's tails",
    "subsample seed 1 only: this varies initialisation and the MC-CV split, not the training draw"
  ],
